:"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"17105005f1f098fe0cc039fce0955f62aba8f90b82e4f60fda1cc7cfa9443be2","event_uuid":"36d7640d-a647-441b-8f66-27e4c0866a0f","position":{"commit_sha":"99194930b37351b76bc1778628cde1cca5339901","position":"1787418411973702001-36d7640d-a647-441b-8f66-27e4c0866a0f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5fa5628aba1565ca531f2d91e630cce85f61bd597476cf33ae47e7941b0ac3e8","event_uuid":"a9f6a393-4e37-49a9-afbc-fb7770ddd21e","position":{"commit_sha":"b5fdc5d652766fa8b0de3e8e11f36b15d6eb6cb1","position":"1787418428121660001-a9f6a393-4e37-49a9-afbc-fb7770ddd21e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6c40926d85b821f789d5df6832f7f9db7afea5a707b1d094d9e122fdcc910afe","event_uuid":"e925415a-2e42-4bb9-8b85-58a748c28711","position":{"commit_sha":"a823d965425de5ac45f27f2717b566d550f85aae","position":"1787419138344009001-e925415a-2e42-4bb9-8b85-58a748c28711"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f0b655d7309bbd68ebb6bf405e1736adb52639fff347244a820445d5d415ada7","event_uuid":"5d3b8068-7a84-4766-accb-cef431cc14d9","position":{"commit_sha":"f43f739ec1a8d39a19185628b95538c192d45712","position":"1787419173255642001-5d3b8068-7a84-4766-accb-cef431cc14d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for blocking finding fe026a21741d96d81: clarified that existing gen_cli_help rendering applies the version-stable usage/metavar normalization contract, both public help entry points serve the exact same committed bytes, and raw argparse fallthrough ends only for registry-declared top-level help owners. Also replaced the representative-route test with registry-driven coverage of all visible canonical intercept routes. Scope remains the ADR 0100 help-discovery slice; no new router, parser, help source, or writing-policy enforcement was added.","timestamp":1787418428121660001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for findings f7933b1b934bcd188, faa324f55e688c487, f6ce8b8cd4fedff2e, f580040ac6aec2172, and f64cc306b459cc6c2: named the concrete helper move into gen_cli_help, removed the independent reference renderer in favor of committed-byte consumption, enumerated the runtime/generator census seams, pinned the exact no-new-metadata ownership predicate, preserved nested argparse fallthrough, and reconciled the two existing overview exemptions. Acceptance checks were split and now cover the preserved branch. The operator-approved rejection of mechanical writing enforcement and the Markdown-only reduced test policy remains explicit and unchanged.","timestamp":1787419173255642001}],"created_at":1787417227306077001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nADR 0100 makes the immutable route registry and parser factories the authority for command identity, grammar, and committed help. Twenty-one visible pure-intercept routes support `rebar <command> --help` but remain absent from overview help and fail under `rebar help <command>`.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the existing help-backed predicate in `scripts/gen_cli_help.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py` exactly `not route.hidden and not route.retired`; do not add a Route metadata field. This includes all twenty-one canonical pure-intercept routes while continuing to exclude hidden aliases and retired spellings.\n- Move `_unwrap_usage` and `_collapse_metavars` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` into `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`. Apply them inside `render_route` only for `route.group == \"intercept\"`, before the existing byte normalization, so new intercept artifacts are stable across Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 while existing non-intercept artifacts retain their byte contract.\n- Generate one committed `help/<route>.txt` artifact for each newly help-backed intercept route. The existing `src/rebar/_cli/_help.py` file lookup, `subcommand_help`, and `known_subcommands` then serve and discover those files without a second rendering path.\n- Update `_help_route.pre_scan` through its mirrored help-backed predicate so leading or top-level pure-intercept help is served before execution. Keep `_NESTED_FAMILY` behavior unchanged: examples such as `rebar bridge preview --help` and `rebar audit serve --help` still fall through to their nested argparse owners, while `rebar audit --help` remains top-level committed help.\n- Delete the live pure-intercept `_render_intercept` path in `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`; make `_syntax_body` use `help_mod.subcommand_help(route.name)` for every documented route and fail if the committed artifact is absent. Thus the reference consumes the exact normalized runtime bytes rather than independently rendering a parser.\n- Retain `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` as exactly `bridge-fsck` and `bridge-probe`, the existing documented compatibility entrypoints already advertised under `bridge`. Retain the matching overview-test allowlist as exactly `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`; none of the twenty-one pure-intercept routes is exempted from overview membership.\n- Regenerate package help, overview help, and the CLI reference through the existing generators.\n- Add registry-driven behavioral coverage for every pure-intercept route, exact-byte equality across both top-level help surfaces, generator determinism, reference consumption, and preserved nested-help fallthrough.\n- Do not add another router, parser, help source, mechanical writing-policy gate, or change to the Markdown-only reduced test policy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live visible route outside the exact documented overview omit set appears exactly once in overview help.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` succeeds for every canonical pure-intercept route returned by the registry.\n- [ ] The registry-driven pure-intercept help test proves no command handler executes.\n- [ ] The registry-driven pure-intercept help test proves no ticket store is mounted or created.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` returns the exact bytes of that route committed artifact.\n- [ ] Top-level `rebar <command> --help` returns the exact bytes of that route committed artifact.\n- [ ] New pure-intercept artifacts render identically under Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13.\n- [ ] Each CLI-reference pure-intercept syntax block equals the corresponding committed artifact rather than a live parser render.\n- [ ] `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` and the test allowlist retain only their named existing bridge/help exemptions; no pure-intercept route is exempt.\n- [ ] Hidden aliases and retired spellings remain absent from overview discovery.\n- [ ] Non-leading nested help for `bridge` and `audit` families retains argparse fallthrough.\n- [ ] Help and CLI-reference drift checks pass.\n- [ ] No competing routing, parser, help, writing-enforcement, or documentation-test-policy mechanism is introduced.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_help.py","reason":"Generate complete visible-route overview artifacts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help.py","reason":"Serve route-owned help for visible intercept commands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py","reason":"Use registry help ownership consistently."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"Regenerate complete overview help."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate complete command discovery reference."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py","reason":"Pin overview membership and generated help."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py","reason":"Pin distributed route and help completeness."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","f7e4-4d33-f231-4774"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["documentation","f12","cli"],"ticket_id":"65c9-aba3-c744-483a","ticket_type":"story","title":"F12 complete ADR 0100 CLI command discovery","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Packaged overview and command help are current"},{"command":"python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Generated CLI reference is current"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py -q","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Route and help distribution contracts pass"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"D4","dd_text":"Source checks pass"}]},"source_event_uuids":["bcf4fd62-dd27-4af4-a4be-13c581c52abd","e6024476-891e-4be0-bdc2-182e7e95bee9","e5476cb4-8a83-4e75-8c7e-173e93655729","36d7640d-a647-441b-8f66-27e4c0866a0f","a9f6a393-4e37-49a9-afbc-fb7770ddd21e","e925415a-2e42-4bb9-8b85-58a748c28711","5d3b8068-7a84-4766-accb-cef431cc14d9"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787419173255642002,"uuid":"07eeccb2-e576-40c4-b14b-2f477a459754"}